msgid "Pompeii was an ancient Roman coastal city, in the Campania region of Italy. Pompeii, along with much of the surrounding area, was mostly destroyed and buried under 4 to 6 meters of volcanic ash and pumice in the eruption of Mount Vesuvius in AD 79."
